splay","line":17},{"title":"Article Views 28547","target":"https://www.mdpi.com/2673-6772/2/3/#metrics","line":18},{"title":"Citations 1","target":"https://www.mdpi.com/2673-6772/2/3/#metrics","line":18},{"title":"Related Info Link","target":"https://www.mdpi.com/2673-6772/2/3/#related","line":18},{"title":"https://doi.org/10.3390/parasitologia2030015","target":"https://doi.org/10.3390/parasitologia2030015","line":46}],"metadata":{"title":"The Tapeworm and Maria Callas’ Diet: A Mystery Revealed","source":"https://www.mdpi.com/2673-6772/2/3/15","author":null,"published":null,"created":"2025-04-28","description":"Maria Callas’ diet, also known as the tapeworm diet, is a non-food-based hazardous treatment. This study aims to justify whether Maria Callas used this treatment for weight loss. To investigate this, we searched in the ‘white’, ‘grey’, and ‘black’ literature. The historical facts about the use of tapeworm pills seem to be inconsistent and include fake news. In the case of Maria Callas, it has been confirmed by her biography and personal communications that she was diagnosed with a beef tapeworm due to eating uncooked meat. This discredits the hypothesis that she consumed tapeworm pills.","tags":[]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"1r6p2rx","at":1778088458060},"key":"Clippings/The Tapeworm and Maria Callas’ Diet A Mystery Revealed.md"},
